WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:04.760
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:10.700
Today, we are not going to create selfies,
we are going to create NERFies instead.

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:11.970
What are those?

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:15.300
Well, NERFies are selfies from the future.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:21.179
The goal here is to take a selfie video, and
turn it into a portrait that we can rotate

00:00:21.179 --> 00:00:23.269
around in complete freedom.

00:00:23.269 --> 00:00:29.340
This technique appeared in November 2020,
a little more than a year ago, and as you

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:32.270
see, it easily outperformed its predecessors.

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:39.240
It shows a lot of strength in these examples
and seems nearly invincible, however, there

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:40.950
is a problem.

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:41.950
What is the problem?

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:46.000
Well, it still did not do all that well on
moving things.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:47.170
Don’t believe it?

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:48.430
Let’s try it out!

00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:50.300
This is the input video.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:51.300
Aha!

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:57.079
There we go, as soon as there is a little
movement in time, we see that it looks like

00:00:57.079 --> 00:01:02.120
a researcher who is about have a powerful
paper deadline experience.

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:06.020
I wonder what the NERFIE technique will do
with this.

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:07.020
Uh-oh.

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:08.990
That’s not optimal.

00:01:08.990 --> 00:01:15.539
And now, let’s see if this new method called
HyperNERF is able to salvage the situation.

00:01:15.539 --> 00:01:16.960
Oh my!

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:22.130
One moment perfectly frozen in time, and we
can move also around with the camera.

00:01:22.130 --> 00:01:26.210
Kind of like the bullet time effect from the
Matrix.

00:01:26.210 --> 00:01:27.540
Sensational.

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:32.750
What is also sensational is that of course,
you Seasoned Fellow Scholars immediately ask

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:37.560
- okay, but which moment will get frozen in
time?

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:40.830
The one with the mouth closed, or open?

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:45.119
And, HyperNERF says, well, you tell me.

00:01:45.119 --> 00:01:50.680
Yes, we can even choose which moment we should
freeze in time by exploring this thing that

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:52.990
they call the hyperspace.

00:01:52.990 --> 00:01:55.109
Hence the name, HyperNERF.

00:01:55.109 --> 00:01:57.170
The process looks like this.

00:01:57.170 --> 00:02:02.799
So, if this can handle animations, well then,
let’s give it some real tough animations.

00:02:02.799 --> 00:02:09.460
This is one of my favorite examples, where
we can even make a video of coffee being made.

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:13.880
Yes, that is indeed the true paper deadline
experience.

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:19.070
And the key to creating these NERFies correctly
is getting this depth map right.

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:24.150
Here, the colors describe how far things are
from the camera.

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:30.100
That is challenging in and of itself, and
now imagine that the camera is moving all

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:31.430
the time too.

00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:37.360
And not only that, but the subject of the
scene is also moving all the time too.

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:41.560
This is very challenging, and this technique
does it just right.

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:46.250
The previous NERFIE technique from just a
year ago had a great deal of trouble with

00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:48.090
this chocolate melting scene.

00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:49.090
Look.

00:02:49.090 --> 00:02:52.650
Tons of artifacts and deformations as we move
the camera.

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:58.960
Now, hold on to your papers and let’s see
if the new method can do even this, now that

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:00.770
would be something…and!

00:03:00.770 --> 00:03:02.100
Wow.

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:03.430
Outstanding.

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:10.690
I also loved how the authors went the extra
mile with the presentation of their website…look!

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:14.480
All the authors are there, animated with this
very method.

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:17.220
Putting their money where their papers are.

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:18.220
Loving it.

00:03:18.220 --> 00:03:20.510
So, with that, there you go.

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:23.820
These are NERFIES, selfies from the future.

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:30.380
And finally, they really work - such amazing
improvements in approximately a year.

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:34.460
The pace of progress in AI research is nothing
short of amazing.

00:03:34.460 --> 00:04:14.970
What a time to be alive!

00:04:14.970 --> 00:04:23.449
Thanks for watching and for your generous
support, and I'll see you next time!

